@startuml
title Use Case 5.3 Open Boards - Main Success Scenario

actor User
participant BoardsView as View
participant OpenBoardController as Controller
participant OpenBoardInteractor as Interactor
participant "JsonBoardDataAccessObject" as BoardDAO
participant "JsonPinDataAccessObject" as PinDAO
participant OpenBoardPresenter as Presenter
participant BoardsViewModel as VM
participant BoardsState as State

User -> View : Select a board from my list
View -> Controller : execute(currentUserId, selectedBoardId)
Controller -> Interactor : execute(inputData)

Interactor -> BoardDAO : findByOwnerAndId(userId, boardId)
BoardDAO --> Interactor : selected board owned by the user
Interactor -> PinDAO : findByOwnerId(userId)
PinDAO --> Interactor : all saved pins owned by the user
Interactor -> Interactor : For each ID in board.getPinIds(),\npick the pin with the same getPinId()
Interactor -> Interactor : Build OpenBoardOutputData with the board name\nand a PinSummary for each match, in board order

Interactor -> Presenter : prepareSuccessView(outputData)
Presenter -> VM : getState()
VM --> Presenter : state
Presenter -> Presenter : Map pin summaries to display cards
Presenter -> State : setOpenedBoard(openedBoard)
Presenter -> VM : notifyStateChanged()
VM -> View : stateChanged()
View -> VM : getState()
VM --> View : state
View -> State : getOpenedBoard()
State --> View : opened board details
View --> User : Display board name and saved pins

' Empty board: skip the pin lookup and present the board name with "No pins yet".
' Missing or unowned board: prepareBoardNotFoundView() and return to the list.
' Board or pin retrieval failure: prepareFailView(error).
@enduml
